  "authorNotes": "KG Maths, 13 sections = 13 syllabus rows, 100 marks. No Mohammadpur 2026 KG final exists; the guide was MP Final 2025 KG Maths, whose questions 1-11 line up almost exactly with the Sylhet rows, so most items are reused verbatim (61-80 in Bangla digits, 81-100 in English, number names 21-50, even/odd sets, ordering sets, column add/subtract, subtraction with lines, matching, 4-times table). MP Half-yearly 2025 KG supplied 'দাগ কেটে যোগ' (row 9), two addition sums for the matching row, and the before/between/after pattern (row 13). Choices the owner may want to check: (1) Rows 1 and 2 (1 x 10) are split into two 5-mark halves (61-70 / 71-80, 81-90 / 91-100) for easier review. (2) Row 6 says both directions: sets ক, গ, ঙ are big-to-small exactly as MP; sets খ and ঘ use MP's numbers but ask small-to-big. Each set has 8 numbers as in MP; trim to 6 if that is too long for KG. (3) Row 11 mixes 3 subtraction and 2 addition sums because the label says যোগ/বিয়োগফল; right-hand column has exactly 5 answers, no extras. (4) Row 12 uses the 4-times table (MP Final 2025 used 4, MP HY used 3); any table 1-5 is in scope. It is split into 10 one-mark lines printed as '৪ × ১ = ___' (the child writes only the product); MP printed an empty grid with just the × sign, so the child wrote the whole line. Pick whichever the school prefers. (5) Row 13 moved most numbers up into 61-100 because the annual scope is 1-100; the last two items are new from book pages 27-28. (6) Rows 2 and 4 are written in English because the syllabus row is in English. Duration '২ ঘণ্টা' is from the MP paper. Book page numbers are printed pages of KG গণিত (2026) unless marked Math (English)."
